WEBVTT

00:41:57.732 --> 00:42:00.907
but is there a sense
that she left in peace

00:42:00.931 --> 00:42:03.854
and a sort of feeling
of some kind of resolution,

00:42:03.878 --> 00:42:08.290
or is it just awful and these are
the kinds of stories

00:42:08.314 --> 00:42:11.704
that we try and tell ourselves after
to try and make life bearable?

00:42:11.728 --> 00:42:14.536
EG: Chris, she was such a badass.

00:42:14.560 --> 00:42:18.581
You know, Rayya was such a warrior.
She never did anything peacefully.

00:42:18.605 --> 00:42:21.575
You know, I came in
with all my, like, yoga ideas,

00:42:21.599 --> 00:42:23.654
and I was like, we're going to orchestrate

00:42:23.678 --> 00:42:25.961
and curate the most
beautiful, peaceful death.

00:42:25.985 --> 00:42:29.642
And that is not what happened, because
that's not what Rayya's life was like,

00:42:29.666 --> 00:42:31.443
and it's not what her death was like.